// ANIMDEFS - texture animations and switch pairs. A text lump at the PK3
// root; GZDoom reads it on top of the engine's own definitions.
// MOD-SPEC 4.3 owns the naming contract; this file pays debt T16.
//
// A `switch` line tells the engine: when a line wearing the OFF texture is
// used (pressed or shot), swap it for the ON texture. Without it SDSW1x is a
// still picture and pressing it changes nothing on the wall.
//
// SYNTAX SOURCE. The ZDoom wiki (https://zdoom.org/wiki/ANIMDEFS) did not
// answer on 2026-10-13, so the syntax is copied from the engine's own file:
// GZDoom g4.14.2, gzdoom.pk3 -> animdefs.txt, lines 194-235, e.g.
//
//     switch doom 1 SW1BRCOM on pic SW2BRCOM tics 0
//
//   switch    keyword: a switch pair follows
//   doom 1    game filter, exactly as the engine writes its Doom switches.
//             `doom` = Doom-family IWADs (Freedoom 2 and Doom II, MOD-SPEC 1);
//             the number is the oldest game the pair exists in (1 shareware,
//             2 registered, 3 Doom II: Doom II's SW1PANEL is `doom 3`).
//             1 is the most permissive tier, so it is used here.
//   SDSW1x    the OFF texture (1 = unpressed, MOD-SPEC 4.3)
//   on pic    the texture shown once the line is used
//   tics 0    the ON state holds that picture; it does not animate
//
// SOUND. None, on purpose. Every Doom switch in the engine's animdefs.txt
// omits `sound` (only the Hexen and Strife lines carry one), and they click
// in game: the engine plays its default switch sound, `switches/normbutn`
// (DSSWTCHN, defined in gzdoom.pk3 -> filter/game-doomchex/sndinfo.txt;
// exit lines get `switches/exitbutn`). Writing `on sound switches/normbutn`
// here would only restate the default. Inferred from that file, NOT VERIFIED
// in the engine source: confirm the click in the PM's engine pass.
//
// Variants (art-director, batch 2, D25): A knife switch, B domed button,
// C slide lever, D hazard panel. tests/test_animdefs.py pins one line per
// pair and tools/check_pk3.py checks every name exists.

switch doom 1 SDSW1A on pic SDSW2A tics 0
switch doom 1 SDSW1B on pic SDSW2B tics 0
switch doom 1 SDSW1C on pic SDSW2C tics 0
switch doom 1 SDSW1D on pic SDSW2D tics 0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Animations (N6c, D66). A `flat` or `texture` definition makes the engine
// swap a surface through its frames on its own, forever: wherever a map uses
// the first frame, the floor or wall cycles 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 1. The
// generator drew each loop seamless, so frame 4 leads back into frame 1.
//
// SYNTAX SOURCE. Read 2026-10-14 in the engine's parser,
// FTextureAnimator::ParseAnim in src/gamedata/textures/animations.cpp (GZDoom
// tag g4.14.2): `flat` and `texture` take the same body, NAME then
// `pic FRAME tics N` per frame (at least two frames); `flat` looks the names
// up as flats, `texture` as walls. VERIFIED in the source; the `texture`
// form is also the one the engine writes itself in gzdoom.pk3 ->
// animdefs.txt (`texture optional M_SKULL1` / `pic M_SKULL1 tics 8`). The
// engine's own file has no `flat` line: Doom's flats animate from the binary
// ANIMATED lump instead. Seen moving in game: NOT VERIFIED (D26).
//
// Every frame is named (`pic`), not `range`: a range takes the frames
// between two names in the texture manager's order, and whether that order
// follows the file names for loose PNGs in a PK3 is NOT VERIFIED; naming
// every frame removes the question. 8 tics = 8/35 s, about 0.23 s a frame, a 0.9 s loop: the
// rate art-director proposed (gen_factory.py previews at GIF_MS = 229, 8
// tics at 35 Hz; docs/art/TEXTURE-INDEX.md). tests/test_animdefs.py
// pins both definitions; tools/check_pk3.py checks every frame is packed.

flat SDMOLT1            // molten metal, the casting pit (flats/factory/)
	pic SDMOLT1 tics 8
	pic SDMOLT2 tics 8
	pic SDMOLT3 tics 8
	pic SDMOLT4 tics 8

texture SDPORT1         // the portal's surface, MAP03's exit (textures/factory/)
	pic SDPORT1 tics 8
	pic SDPORT2 tics 8
	pic SDPORT3 tics 8
	pic SDPORT4 tics 8
